1
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:55,640
You're awake.

2
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:59,000
Perfect timing.
I was just about to make breakfast.

3
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,480
How about I make it instead?

4
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:06,160
Consider it my way
of thanking you for hosting me.

5
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,640
Does that mean I'm getting a feast?

6
00:02:09,919 --> 00:02:11,480
You're an international student,

7
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:13,440
so you must have
instant noodles at home, right?

8
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:16,840
Growing up, the best thing I could
ever cook was instant noodles.

9
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:19,280
Do you want to try?

10
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:24,360
I make incredible poached eggs too.
They never fall apart.

11
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,520
Impressive.

12
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,240
Why does that sound so sarcastic?

13
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:35,480
That's unfair.
I was clearly expressing my admiration.

14
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,320
If you don't believe me,
we can have a cook-off.

15
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,920
We'll each make a bowl.

16
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:44,280
You want to compete over this too?

17
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:46,960
I'm just trying to learn from
your admirable qualities.

18
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:49,680
Back when we joined the lab
and competed for the Vitality Award,

19
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,760
didn't you say
we shouldn't try to cozy up,

20
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,360
but should compete properly instead?

21
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:55,120
That was ages ago.

22
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,640
Are we doing this or not?

23
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,120
All right. Whatever you say.

24
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:03,920
You're cheating.

25
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,480
It's called the competitive spirit.

26
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,320
So which bowl do you want?

27
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:23,360
Aren't we being a little childish?

28
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:25,440
Don't drag me into this.

29
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,080
Even if we are, it's because of you.

30
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,240
I'll admit that.

31
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:36,720
By the way, I want to go back to the dorm
to check on things.

32
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,600
I have to resolve
the situation eventually.

33
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,520
- I'll go with you.
- It's okay.

34
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:44,240
Trust me. I can handle it myself.

35
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:20,920
What are you doing here?

36
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:23,680
Were you worried I couldn't handle it?

37
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:28,240
Not worried. Just concerned.

38
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:31,240
Are you hungry?

39
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:32,680
Let's get something to eat first.

40
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:41,120
That Theresa was completely out of line.

41
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:43,840
She tried to make me pay
the fire alarm response fee.

42
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,120
And then?

43
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:48,360
After a battle of words,
she didn't get a single cent from me.

44
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:50,200
She even apologized.

45
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:51,120
You're amazing.

46
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:55,800
But since she apologized,
paid the compensation,

47
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:57,000
and showed a decent attitude,

48
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:59,120
plus she has an active lease contract,

49
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:03,040
the dorm manager has no plans
to ask her to move out or evict her.

50
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,840
Even if she left, I'd still be worried
about your safety living there.

51
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:09,240
After all, they know where you live.

52
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:14,800
Actually, I'm not surprised at all
that you handled it well.

53
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:16,280
That's just how you are.

54
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:19,280
You've always shouldered everything alone
and solved problems by yourself.

55
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,600
Then why ask so many questions?

56
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:24,320
Because I want to hear you talk.

57
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:26,400
If you're willing to speak,
I'll always listen.

58
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:30,280
But I want you to know

59
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,440
that you're not alone.

60
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:36,040
Whenever and wherever you need me,

61
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,200
I'll be there.

62
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:45,200
And of course,
even if you don't need me,

63
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:46,320
I'll still be around.

64
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:48,680
At worst, just waiting nearby.

65
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:52,680
Got it.

66
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:53,840
Don't worry.

67
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:57,000
I won't compromise myself
by continuing to live there.

68
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:58,840
There's no way I'm living
with someone like her.

69
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:02,720
Then

70
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,600
what would your ideal roommate be like?

71
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:11,200
Actually, I'm not asking for much.

72
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:15,040
First, they have to be clean
and not leave trash lying around.

73
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:17,480
Second, they should keep regular hours

74
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:20,000
and not bring random people back home.

75
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,800
I can accept pretty much anything else.

76
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:26,280
But since we're talking about
an ideal roommate,

77
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,480
I'll add one more thing.

78
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,560
We should get along well.

79
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,720
Do I qualify to be your roommate then?

80
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,040
I'd like to apply for the position.

81
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:46,440
And if possible,
I hope to be your ideal one.

82
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:49,600
Besides everything you just listed,

83
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,200
I can also make you breakfast every day.

84
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:55,520
Of course, I'll have to
work on my poached eggs.

85
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:58,440
If you ever get bored,

86
00:06:58,520 --> 00:06:59,920
we can watch movies together.

87
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,680
I'm fine with any genre.

88
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:05,120
Or we can go for walks together.

89
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,480
I know Berlin pretty well.

90
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:15,000
Why does this sound
so much like a job interview?

91
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,360
So is my application approved?

92
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:21,760
Approved.

93
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,480
Great!

94
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,400
In that case,

95
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:28,080
my dear roommate,

96
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,760
come somewhere with me tomorrow.

97
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,080
This is…

98
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:47,040
Our new home.

99
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,600
The old apartment
was close to the research institute,

100
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:51,760
but it took you an hour to get to school.

101
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:54,320
This place is right in the middle.

102
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:55,680
It's perfect.

103
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:59,440
Besides, I'd been wanting to move anyway.

104
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:01,840
I couldn't just keep staying
in that place forever.

105
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:07,040
I have some money I made from investments
saved, so I decided to get a bigger place.

106
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:08,920
Investments?

107
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,760
A few senior classmates and I
invested in a biotech startup.

108
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:15,320
We got lucky. The company was acquired.

109
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,480
It's no fortune,

110
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:19,400
but renting this place
definitely won't be a problem.

111
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:23,160
When did you start looking for places?

112
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:26,800
Yesterday, before I picked you up.

113
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:31,640
You already sent me the offer letter.
You can't take it back now.

114
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:34,400
Come on. Let me show you around.

115
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,600
Here's the kitchen.

116
00:08:37,679 --> 00:08:38,919
It's pretty spacious.

117
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,559
The oven and dishwasher
are both brand-new.

118
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:43,280
Here's the master bedroom.

119
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:45,200
The natural light is
especially nice in winter.

120
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:46,880
This entire side will get plenty of sun.

121
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,720
And here's the closet.

122
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:53,240
No matter how many clothes you have,
there'll be plenty of room for them.

123
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:56,560
Here's the balcony.

124
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:59,160
We can plant some greenery here.

125
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:02,040
On nice sunny days,
lounging here with a good book

126
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:03,320
is going to feel so comfortable.

127
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:05,600
Chen Yanzhou.

128
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:08,840
Aren't you tired?

129
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:10,720
Not at all.

130
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:12,400
You're lying.

131
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:15,160
You must have put
a lot of effort into this place.

132
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,400
How about this?

133
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:19,040
When we move, you supervise
while I do the heavy lifting.

134
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:21,240
How could I let you do that?

135
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:23,040
This is an order, my roommate.

136
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:25,920
As you command.

137
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,440
How is everything already packed up?

138
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:03,440
You didn't wait for me?

139
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,400
Didn't I tell you?

140
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:08,280
You just need to supervise
and I'll do the heavy lifting.

141
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,960
You never said I couldn't help.

142
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,920
Still working this late?

143
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:24,040
No.

144
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,600
I just need to upload a few files.

145
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:37,960
What's wrong?

146
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:41,600
Nothing.

147
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,040
Chen Yanzhou.

148
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:25,040
Where are you sleeping tonight?

149
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:30,440
The sofa.

150
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:50,360
We still have to move tomorrow,
so get some rest.

151
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,080
Where's my pillow?

152
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:02,120
I don't know. What pillow?

153
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,640
The one I use on the sofa.

154
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:10,560
I might've packed it in one of the boxes.

155
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,120
You packed it?

156
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:27,280
Okay, I'll look for it.

157
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,200
Wait.

158
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:34,080
Last time, you gave me
one of your pillows.

159
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:36,240
I have two in my room.
I'll get you one.

160
00:12:38,680 --> 00:12:40,360
Well, thanks then.

161
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:55,760
Good night.

162
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:58,040
Good night.

163
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:17,680
<i>Zheng Yu.</i>

164
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:19,720
<i>Are you hiding something from us?</i>

165
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:22,320
XU FANGLI

166
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:23,680
<i>Can I ask you something?</i>

167
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:27,160
<i>If there is someone you actively approach</i>
<i>and they respond,</i>

168
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:28,880
<i>but won't take things any further,</i>

169
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:30,000
<i>why is that?</i>

170
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:35,600
<i>What kind of "actively approach"</i>
<i>and "take things any further" do you mean?</i>

171
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:41,840
<i>Just forget it.</i>

172
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:49,520
<i>I knew it!</i>

173
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,720
<i>You didn't send that message</i>
<i>by mistake last time.</i>

174
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,800
<i>Why so quiet all of a sudden?</i>

175
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:01,640
<i>Did you fall asleep again?</i>

176
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:06,640
<i>You're going to make me</i>
<i>lose sleep over this.</i>

177
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,120
<i>I'm going to sleep.</i>

178
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,160
<i>I have to</i>
<i>move tomorrow,</i>

179
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:11,040
<i>and there's still</i>
<i>a lot to do.</i>

180
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,040
Why are you copying me?

181
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:11,520
A new home calls for a fresh look.

182
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:14,240
Look. Doesn't it look much better
arranged this way?

183
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,440
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

184
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:35,800
<i>You said you were moving.</i>
<i>Where are you moving to?</i>

185
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:39,280
<i>And about that question you asked,</i>
<i>I've given it some more thought.</i>

186
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:41,440
<i>Could he be into platonic love?</i>

187
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:53,760
What's wrong?

188
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:56,360
Nothing.

189
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:26,400
It really feels like a real home now.

190
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:29,320
It already is a home.

191
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:45,880
What's wrong?

192
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:49,480
Nothing. I'm just happy.

193
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:07,280
What are you…?

194
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:09,360
I'm sleeping on the sofa.

195
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:16,600
The power's out.

196
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:18,880
Stay right there. Don't move.

197
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:48,680
It's probably a building management issue.

198
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:51,760
We only signed the papers yesterday, so
there's probably still things to sort out.

199
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:55,520
So what do we do?

200
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,040
We'll just have to make do tonight.

201
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:01,040
I'll have the landlord
take care of it tomorrow.

202
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:38,800
Chen Yanzhou, do you remember the trip
we went on for our field practice?

203
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:41,120
I went out, and you came looking for me.

204
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,120
We were at the campsite,

205
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:44,640
just like this.

206
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:47,400
I remember.

207
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:50,320
But it's not raining today.

208
00:19:58,200 --> 00:19:59,360
The power's out.

209
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:00,880
We can't really do anything.

210
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:05,080
I have some movies
downloaded on my computer.

211
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:06,800
We could watch one if you liked?

212
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:09,400
I'll get it then.

213
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:28,840
<i>And about that question you asked,</i>
<i>I've given it some more thought.</i>

214
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:31,800
<i>Could he be into platonic love?</i>

215
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,400
Chen Yanzhou.

216
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:45,560
Are you… into platonic love?

217
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:53,120
You always stop halfway through kissing,

218
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:55,240
and you sleep on the sofa every night.

219
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:57,560
Xu Fangli said…

220
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:01,880
I didn't tell her about us
or mention your name.

221
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:04,280
It just came up in conversation.

222
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:07,080
She said that in situations
like this, usually…

223
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:29,200
Zheng Yu.

224
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,360
Are you joking?

225
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:35,440
I'm serious.

226
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:39,600
Then what gave you
such a huge misconception?

227
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:42,200
Didn't I just tell you?

228
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:44,240
Every time you kiss,
you stop halfway through…

229
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,560
What did you say?

230
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:54,680
You always stop
halfway through kissing,

231
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:56,360
and you sleep
on the sofa every night.

232
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:58,040
It's the same today.

233
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:01,120
Haven't you noticed

234
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:03,800
that I've been holding back
this whole time?

235
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:06,400
I've been waiting for you to be ready.

236
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:10,360
Even today?

237
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:54,000
It's raining.

238
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:57,360
Don't get distracted.

239
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:32,160
Morning.

240
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:33,120
Morning.

241
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:36,720
Did you sleep well last night?

242
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:41,640
I can tell.

243
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:43,080
Look at your bedhead.

244
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:53,960
XIAOMIAN

245
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:55,280
It's Xiaomian.

246
00:23:55,360 --> 00:23:57,320
What… do I do?

247
00:23:57,400 --> 00:23:59,240
- I…
- Perfect timing. Answer it.

248
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:01,400
I haven't talked to him in ages.

249
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:03,040
Let me chat with him later for a bit.

250
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:10,160
You…

251
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:12,880
Are you planning to…?

252
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:16,760
I'm not ready
to tell Xiaomian about us yet.

253
00:24:16,840 --> 00:24:18,640
Could you step away for a bit?

254
00:24:26,120 --> 00:24:27,240
Never mind.

255
00:24:27,320 --> 00:24:29,600
Conveniently enough,
I have a few emails to take care of.

256
00:24:45,560 --> 00:24:47,800
<i>Surprise, Ms. Zheng!</i>

257
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:49,120
Gao Xing?

258
00:24:57,760 --> 00:24:59,760
Why are you using Xiaomian's phone?

259
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:02,560
<i>He's free on weekends,</i>
<i>so I asked him to tutor me.</i>

260
00:25:02,640 --> 00:25:05,160
<i>Let me tell you, he is super strict!</i>

261
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,160
<i>He makes me study all day.</i>

262
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:08,480
<i>Time's up. Get back to your exercises.</i>

263
00:25:09,600 --> 00:25:10,800
<i>I have my own phone too.</i>

264
00:25:12,080 --> 00:25:14,800
<i>I'll talk to you again</i>
<i>once I finish my homework, Ms. Zheng.</i>

265
00:25:14,880 --> 00:25:15,880
Okay.

266
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:19,480
<i>Zheng Yu, why did you</i>
<i>take so long to answer?</i>

267
00:25:20,440 --> 00:25:22,560
I didn't hear it ringing.

268
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:25,960
<i>What were you doing?</i>
<i>How could you not hear it?</i>

269
00:25:29,960 --> 00:25:33,160
<i>Is it hot in your dorm?</i>
<i>Or is it the lighting?</i>

270
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,920
<i>Why is your face so red?</i>

271
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:36,880
I…

272
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:41,560
It suddenly got cold recently,
so they've turned on the heating indoors.

273
00:25:41,640 --> 00:25:43,120
<i>They turned on the heat this early?</i>

274
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:45,440
<i>Make sure to dress warmly when you go out.</i>

275
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:46,960
Okay.

276
00:25:47,040 --> 00:25:48,440
<i>Zheng Yu.</i>

277
00:25:48,520 --> 00:25:50,840
<i>Now that you're over there,</i>
<i>have you seen Yanzhou?</i>

278
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:56,520
I haven't had a chance to see him yet.

279
00:25:56,600 --> 00:25:57,880
He's been pretty busy lately.

280
00:25:59,760 --> 00:26:02,520
<i>I thought he'd be really happy</i>
<i>to see you there.</i>

281
00:26:02,600 --> 00:26:03,480
<i>Never mind.</i>

282
00:26:03,560 --> 00:26:06,000
<i>It's already been a year.</i>
<i>People change, after all.</i>

283
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:08,600
<i>Zheng Yu, just ignore him.</i>

284
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:12,120
<i>What was that noise?</i>

285
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:15,920
My roommate. I don't know
what's wrong with them.

286
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:19,960
<i>Roommate? Is that the weird roommate</i>
<i>you were talking about?</i>

287
00:26:20,040 --> 00:26:22,160
No, that roommate has moved out.

288
00:26:22,240 --> 00:26:24,920
Don't worry. The person living with me now
is my new roommate.

289
00:26:26,120 --> 00:26:29,800
My new roommate is a really good person.

290
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:34,160
Even when I sometimes go a little too far,

291
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:38,240
that person is incredibly understanding
and would never hold it against me.

292
00:26:38,320 --> 00:26:39,640
<i>That's good then.</i>

293
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:42,520
<i>Zheng Yu, it must be mealtime over there.</i>

294
00:26:42,600 --> 00:26:43,520
<i>I won't keep you.</i>

295
00:26:44,560 --> 00:26:45,400
All right.

296
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:47,880
Let's talk again if anything comes up.

297
00:26:47,960 --> 00:26:48,960
<i>Bye.</i>

298
00:26:50,080 --> 00:26:51,320
Bye.

299
00:26:52,800 --> 00:26:53,680
Where are you going?

300
00:26:55,920 --> 00:26:56,760
To get chopsticks.

301
00:27:01,800 --> 00:27:03,800
Are you mad?

302
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:12,120
I was just worried that
if I told Xiaomian we'd met,

303
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:15,440
he'd start asking questions
and find out we're living together.

304
00:27:15,520 --> 00:27:16,920
So I…

305
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:21,560
I was wrong.

306
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:29,800
"People change, after all.
Just ignore him."

307
00:27:31,600 --> 00:27:34,480
So that's the kind of guy I am
in Xiaomian's eyes now.

308
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:37,160
And someone here
can't even help clear things up for me.

309
00:27:37,240 --> 00:27:41,520
Then I'll call him right now
and tell him we've seen each other.

310
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:44,440
And not only that,
we're living together now.

311
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:49,720
And right before he called,
we were kissing.

312
00:27:53,200 --> 00:27:55,160
Let's be precise. We didn't actually kiss.

313
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:17,800
This make-up effort of yours
is way too half-hearted.

314
00:28:19,120 --> 00:28:20,840
Half-hearted?

315
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:23,360
Just how terrible of a sin did I commit?

316
00:28:25,840 --> 00:28:27,040
A huge one.

317
00:28:28,360 --> 00:28:29,320
How about…

318
00:28:30,160 --> 00:28:31,080
I throw this in too?

319
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:43,320
It's Gao Xing.

320
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:47,680
I should answer it.

321
00:28:49,720 --> 00:28:50,600
Let me answer it.

322
00:28:56,160 --> 00:28:58,280
<i>Ms. Zheng, I'm done with my exercises!</i>

323
00:28:58,360 --> 00:28:59,680
Gao Xing, I--

324
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:02,600
Gao Xing, my girlfriend's
private time is very expensive.

325
00:29:02,680 --> 00:29:05,240
From now on, every minute will
be deducted from your New Year's money.

326
00:29:05,320 --> 00:29:07,400
- If you agree, keep talking.
- You…

327
00:29:08,520 --> 00:29:09,360
She hung up.

328
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,040
You…

329
00:29:12,120 --> 00:29:13,520
What are you doing?

330
00:29:13,600 --> 00:29:17,200
I was just trying to tease her.
Who knew she'd get scared so easily?

331
00:29:18,520 --> 00:29:20,320
As her older cousin,
how could you do that to her?

332
00:29:21,400 --> 00:29:23,960
All right. I'll send her
a red packet later to make it up to her.

333
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:25,960
- Let's eat.
- You…

334
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:28,600
Otherwise, you'll be late for class.

335
00:30:34,280 --> 00:30:37,560
Tomato…

336
00:30:37,640 --> 00:30:38,960
What are you muttering to yourself?

337
00:30:39,800 --> 00:30:42,680
I'm memorizing German words
for the things I need to buy later.

338
00:30:44,960 --> 00:30:46,760
Isn't there a teacher
standing right next to you?

339
00:30:48,200 --> 00:30:49,760
So how do you say tomato?

340
00:30:49,840 --> 00:30:50,760
<i>Tomate?</i>

341
00:30:50,840 --> 00:30:51,920
<i>Tomate</i>.

342
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:53,120
<i>Tomate</i>.

343
00:30:53,200 --> 00:30:55,200
- Lemon?
<i>- Zitrone</i>.

344
00:30:57,440 --> 00:30:59,360
Passionfruit?

345
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:01,440
<i>Die Maracuja</i>.

346
00:31:04,560 --> 00:31:06,440
What about Brussels sprouts?

347
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:07,800
I bet you don't know that one.

348
00:31:08,640 --> 00:31:09,840
<i>Der Rosenkohl.</i>

349
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:11,320
What else do you want to know?

350
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:15,160
My name, Zheng Yu.

351
00:31:15,240 --> 00:31:16,520
How do you say my name?

352
00:31:19,400 --> 00:31:20,800
<i>Regenschauer</i>.

353
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:22,440
It means a passing shower in Chinese.

354
00:31:22,520 --> 00:31:23,720
"<i>Regenschauer</i>."

355
00:31:24,600 --> 00:31:26,480
What about Chen Yanzhou?

356
00:31:31,520 --> 00:31:33,720
<i>Die Liebe meines Lebens</i>.

357
00:31:34,600 --> 00:31:37,280
"<i>Die Liebe meines Lebens</i>."

358
00:31:40,720 --> 00:31:41,840
Why are you laughing?

359
00:31:41,920 --> 00:31:43,240
Was my pronunciation wrong?

360
00:31:43,320 --> 00:31:44,880
Your pronunciation was perfect.

361
00:31:44,960 --> 00:31:46,240
Say it again.

362
00:31:46,320 --> 00:31:48,480
<i>Die Liebe meines Lebens</i>.

363
00:31:53,560 --> 00:31:56,160
<i>Die Liebe meines Lebens</i>.

364
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:00,960
THE LOVE OF MY LIFE

365
00:32:02,560 --> 00:32:03,720
Chen Yanzhou.

366
00:32:03,800 --> 00:32:04,720
You tricked me!

367
00:32:06,240 --> 00:32:07,240
Why are you hitting me?

368
00:32:07,320 --> 00:32:08,480
Am I not the love of your life?

369
00:32:08,560 --> 00:32:10,800
How can you hit
the person you love the most?

370
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:14,200
I hit you because I feel like it!
You're so childish!

371
00:32:14,280 --> 00:32:15,560
Don't you run!

372
00:32:16,600 --> 00:32:17,960
Okay, I'll stop.

373
00:32:22,040 --> 00:32:23,480
Look at that pear.

374
00:32:23,560 --> 00:32:24,680
It's so tiny and cute!

375
00:32:24,760 --> 00:32:26,280
This one?

376
00:32:26,360 --> 00:32:29,160
The mangoes are cute too,
all nice and red.

377
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:32,080
Strawberries!

378
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:41,400
Chen Yanzhou,
why are you getting so much fruit?

379
00:32:44,800 --> 00:32:45,960
To bribe you.

380
00:32:46,560 --> 00:32:47,640
To bribe me?

381
00:32:48,520 --> 00:32:50,280
Come meet someone with me tomorrow.

382
00:32:51,320 --> 00:32:52,680
Who?

383
00:32:52,760 --> 00:32:54,640
You'll know tomorrow.
It's very important.

384
00:33:13,520 --> 00:33:15,400
Who are you taking me to meet?

385
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:16,480
A Chinese person?

386
00:33:17,440 --> 00:33:18,400
A German person.

387
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:20,960
A woman?

388
00:33:25,560 --> 00:33:27,560
What kind of woman?

389
00:33:31,720 --> 00:33:32,680
She

390
00:33:33,480 --> 00:33:34,960
is blonde,

391
00:33:35,040 --> 00:33:36,600
very tall,

392
00:33:36,680 --> 00:33:38,360
and incredibly elegant.

393
00:33:38,440 --> 00:33:39,720
She also speaks fluent English.

394
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:43,400
We used to discuss art
and philosophy together.

395
00:33:48,240 --> 00:33:49,200
Why?

396
00:33:49,800 --> 00:33:50,880
Are you jealous?

397
00:33:51,880 --> 00:33:53,400
I'm not.

398
00:33:53,480 --> 00:33:54,400
Keep going.

399
00:34:00,240 --> 00:34:01,800
She also likes these kinds of tulips.

400
00:34:02,440 --> 00:34:05,000
She said they remind her
of the gardens back home.

401
00:34:13,960 --> 00:34:16,360
She's practically eaten
at every restaurant in Berlin.

402
00:34:16,440 --> 00:34:18,400
She's the one
who recommended this place to me.

403
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:20,920
Of everyone I've ever met,

404
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:22,159
she knows the most about food.

405
00:34:22,239 --> 00:34:25,320
Everyone who meets her
is immediately drawn to her.

406
00:34:26,719 --> 00:34:28,560
Who on earth is she?

407
00:34:30,400 --> 00:34:31,320
She's here.

408
00:34:47,560 --> 00:34:49,719
Eleonore was my very first professor
when I came to Berlin.

409
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:52,440
She retired at the end of last year
and left the research institute.

410
00:34:52,520 --> 00:34:54,360
This is her husband, Karl.

411
00:35:38,920 --> 00:35:40,400
Karl is a very romantic man.

412
00:35:41,120 --> 00:35:42,240
"<i>Lang man</i>."

413
00:37:01,760 --> 00:37:04,240
But aren't you joining
your professor's project group?

414
00:37:04,320 --> 00:37:07,000
- Will you have enough time?
- It's fine.

415
00:38:46,600 --> 00:38:49,200
We probably should have
walked Eleonore and Karl back.

416
00:38:49,280 --> 00:38:50,600
It's so dark out now.

417
00:38:52,400 --> 00:38:53,240
It's fine.

418
00:38:53,320 --> 00:38:56,120
They like taking walks together,
just like we're doing now.

419
00:38:57,560 --> 00:38:58,600
That's sweet.

420
00:38:58,680 --> 00:39:01,000
They've been walking together
for almost 50 years

421
00:39:01,080 --> 00:39:02,840
and they can still
take a walk home together.

422
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:07,120
Looks like we need to practice hard too.

423
00:39:07,680 --> 00:39:08,640
Practice for what?

424
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:10,560
For 50 years of walking together.

425
00:39:11,480 --> 00:39:12,920
I remember back at the Sports Meet,

426
00:39:13,000 --> 00:39:15,120
you ran the 1500 m
and then did the 3000 m right after!

427
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:18,800
Walking for 60 or 70 years
shouldn't be a problem at all.

428
00:39:30,800 --> 00:39:33,600
By the way, are you going
to the lab this weekend?

429
00:39:33,680 --> 00:39:34,600
Yes.

430
00:39:34,680 --> 00:39:36,480
My advisor is going on
a business trip next week,

431
00:39:36,560 --> 00:39:38,000
so our group meeting got moved up.

432
00:39:40,640 --> 00:39:42,600
What's wrong? Do you have plans?

433
00:39:43,880 --> 00:39:44,720
No, it's nothing.

434
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:47,640
Let's go home and get some sleep!

435
00:40:33,960 --> 00:40:35,240
ZHENG YU

436
00:40:35,320 --> 00:40:37,640
<i>I'll be working late today,</i>
<i>so don't wait up for me.</i>

437
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:58,000
DORM 223 LET'S GO

438
00:40:58,080 --> 00:41:00,360
<i>Zheng Yu, happy birthday!</i>

439
00:41:00,440 --> 00:41:02,560
<i>Happy birthday!</i>

440
00:41:02,640 --> 00:41:05,320
<i>Is anyone celebrating with you?</i>

441
00:41:05,400 --> 00:41:08,200
<i>Happy birthday, Zheng Yu!</i>

442
00:41:09,880 --> 00:41:11,160
That's right.

443
00:41:11,240 --> 00:41:12,360
It's my birthday today.

444
00:41:12,440 --> 00:41:14,480
<i>Where's Zheng Yu?</i>

445
00:41:14,560 --> 00:41:15,520
<i>She's probably asleep.</i>

446
00:41:15,600 --> 00:41:17,600
<i>It's nighttime in Berlin right now.</i>

447
00:41:20,840 --> 00:41:24,840
XU FANGLI: HAPPY BIRTHDAY, ZHENG YU

448
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:26,400
<i>It's bait for the fish.</i>

449
00:41:27,320 --> 00:41:29,280
<i>Why isn't the fish taking the bait?</i>

450
00:41:33,800 --> 00:41:35,640
<i>Zheng Yu, happy birthday!</i>

451
00:41:35,720 --> 00:41:39,120
<i>Ms. Zheng, I heard</i>
<i>from someone that it's your birthday.</i>

452
00:41:39,200 --> 00:41:41,520
<i>Happy birthday!</i>

453
00:41:41,600 --> 00:41:43,640
<i>Did Yanzhou buy you a cake?</i>

454
00:41:43,720 --> 00:41:47,960
<i>Don't worry.</i>
<i>I won't tell anyone about the two of you.</i>

455
00:41:48,040 --> 00:41:49,320
<i>Are you still at the lab?</i>

456
00:41:49,400 --> 00:41:50,560
CHEN YANZHOU

457
00:41:50,640 --> 00:41:53,040
<i>By the way, are you going</i>
<i>to the lab this weekend?</i>

458
00:41:53,120 --> 00:41:55,920
<i>Yes. My advisor is going on</i>
<i>a business trip next week,</i>

459
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:57,600
<i>so our group meeting got moved up.</i>

460
00:42:07,040 --> 00:42:07,880
Hello?

461
00:44:52,160 --> 00:44:57,160
Subtitle translation by: Cempaka Malinja
